			"claims": [
				{
					"id": "correction:15a28e560194b0de108ae4fb20096ea1a92e9dbc1a593d99cc3132592efa3bd1",
					"reason": "The exact repaired spectral card is supported by the supplied fractional-domain proof. Both low modes, sine normalization, all-member coefficient asymptotics and endpoint divergence are correct. The formerly unresolved window is closed by a separate four-trace graph-core argument, with individual membership distinguished from compatible finite combinations.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:6d468ed87a736afdfb81282b1d434d5c0b16a920a59116ca2c4738896d7184f7",
					"reason": "Negative orders are correctly defined by completion rather than by assigning a weaker norm to the unchanged L2 set. Spectral multiplication gives the stated isometries on the completed scale. Positive-order statements retain the strictly positive self-adjoint hypothesis, and the exact spectral dependency includes both affine modes.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:76ae1aa768a6db16a98db28fb5b738ff2d8556317bb1bd50086601d9ca04b2ed",
					"reason": "The source and dependency hashes match the supplied repaired versions. The added 0<=s<7/2 statement concerns the fixed Krein operator and follows from the reviewed graph-core proof; it does not enlarge the hypotheses of the general left-definite theory.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:aa949b7a06836d9ea2713484de2548807e0043e6c6600c5c6c4ce3ced54af7d8",
					"reason": "The moment-jump argument now explicitly requires membership, pinned low moments, both parity chains, B_j>=0 and A_j-B_j>=4j+c0. Monotonicity and multiplication of ratio lower bounds yield (4/c0)^(j-1)j!, contradicting the stated moment bounds. Mere positivity of the coefficient difference is not used to infer factorial growth.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:c7080ba7c2ef1b2033b7dcb62e969e37acc23221d74722681cced2d7e1e80794",
					"reason": "The expanded density window is explicitly attributed to the independently checked four-trace argument. The card does not extend its moment method to undefined higher-order monomial pairings, and it retains the obstruction at s=7/2.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:6bd2127271b8002ba3f637e9fcfa27573d02f993a06ab4405ca1fce982db8440",
					"reason": "The recurrence method is restricted to s=2,3, where the descended spaces L2 and the first form domain contain the required monomials. Both parity coefficients have difference 4m+cm/(m-1), so the stronger growth hypothesis holds. Domain membership is required before operator transport, and the old all-order conclusion remains withdrawn.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:d5c986e8260e6d53b4e310fb6eff66de8692cdc2079abf36784819368f6ae527",
					"reason": "The updated spectral dependency and fractional source have the declared hashes. The card correctly separates its s=2,3 recurrence proof from the new density proof for 3<s<7/2, without identifying formal differentiation or a polynomial algebraic inverse with genuine operator powers.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:26407866b3eb4034b240ff741a3d270995ad4a1c49b5ebbeb70a2bf89c85151a",
					"reason": "The abstract criteria retain polynomial membership and density as hypotheses, require both parity chains, and distinguish sufficient growth conditions from the diagonal-space classification. The identity span{p_n}=Pi intersect D(Kc), of algebraic codimension two in Pi, is correct. These hypotheses are not imposed without justification on higher Krein domains.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:22f146c8cda5ae02aad6c635fc0226ec7b8e14c846f6ef9be736be149d692380",
					"reason": "The current range update follows from the reviewed source and preserves the abstract criteria's hypotheses. The projection qualification is sound: polynomial density alone does not imply sparse-family density, while adjoining x^2,x^3 fills the algebraic deficit. A finite collection of scalar tests cannot be injective on a space containing an infinite linearly independent tail.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:dfe69aac1cc39c7aba7abc9859d24499f6a52e756a4ad0ec32d81a0dfdaea3e7",
					"reason": "The current card uses the correct first-derivative Krein boundary conditions, records H2/H3 density consistently with the supplied proofs, and withdraws the all-order polynomial interpretation. The explicit algebraic inverse of x^2 violates those boundary conditions, whereas the genuine inverse includes the required hyperbolic correction.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:8a7029b0cb118701bbba702e962f82d2cb96cce31de7ef87f95ccab72b400bb2",
					"reason": "The supplied quotient proof correctly gives the zero-parameter Gram diagonal 2(2n-1). Ordinary H1 limits are P2/sqrt(6), P3/sqrt(10), and Q_n for n>=4; all corresponding quotient limits are [Q_n]. The parity induction uses an O_n(a_n) remainder, with a6-(63/c)a4=1+42/c confirming why O(1) is invalid. The assertions remain fixed-index statements.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:4642df3b2057e258d4056d26a993ce0165e3576b022d0af60deec33e7ab4c6f3",
					"reason": "The repaired card accurately propagates the fixed-c window and every nonaffine named member's exclusion for s>=7/2. It permits boundary cancellation in finite combinations and keeps the c-to-zero quotient analysis separate. Its quotient and inverse-obstruction source hashes match the supplied snapshots.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:c704f0b5443243081c96a35469d3649aadace73278c4f2427ecbd550bb77cbf9",
					"reason": "The general recurrence supplies only a product lower bound; exact product classifications are restricted to B=B'=0, and the diagonal criterion uses both actual recurrence solutions. Perturbations correctly change both A and B. The all-index bound |delta_m|<=1/(8m) gives A-B>=(7/2)m+c, while the displayed P2 annihilator correctly demonstrates failure of unconditional bounded-perturbation completeness.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:458a02186e9a8e23d76fc42be0faa4d9943d5e073d578c5c72a31781c20a6d4c",
					"reason": "The stability source has the same SHA-256 as the binding in the supplied earlier card. Its recurrence, model and perturbation arguments were checked directly and do not depend on the repaired quotient-limit assertion. The binding renewal therefore introduces no new stability assumption.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:ff0ab3ad28d7a31f6dded0143b838518577b9efa30c664c2882acdf985e88ac7",
					"reason": "The current range statement points to the valid four-trace proof. It does not identify the abstract diagonal spaces with Krein domains or extend the conditional stability results to arbitrary perturbations or stable bases.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:4660445eefe6a76a2b70658964d090a0e893c9026ec4f396c040753b038c9124",
					"reason": "The structural card works in complex Hc2=D(Kc), with the actual boundary conditions and norm ||Kc f||2. Both low trace directions are retained, and the genuine isometric inverse is justified by positivity and surjectivity. Neither negative-order completion nor the enlarged full-family range is used to assert tail rigidity.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:cee93c289836f3d9d4fb197a917cfe93c205619d43e7a2b9d1a5d7bdb500126b",
					"reason": "The repaired cofinite theorem follows from the tail algebra, local H2 cutoff estimates and vanishing endpoint corrections. The Green functions have the required interface jumps and represent f(0),f'(0), with correct complex conjugation. The closure depends exactly on retention of indices 0 and 1. The monomial deletion argument using x^M f also repairs the odd-factor error without transferring its conclusion to the image family.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:e99563a533bc6c760da7a90f9327742d52c8000206f0f963fb98d1fa5be54e44",
					"reason": "The upstream dependency is updated to the exact supplied left-definite card. The cofinite proof source retains its earlier recorded hash, and its classification remains restricted to s=2. Full-family density on 0<=s<7/2 is not used to classify deleted families at other orders or arbitrary constrained spaces.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "R6-complete-spectrum-and-all-member-threshold",
					"reason": "Integration by parts establishes Kc>=cI; the explicit homogeneous boundary matrix is invertible for c>0, giving surjectivity and self-adjointness. The H2 estimate gives compact inverse. Solving both parity problems yields exactly the two affine modes and the stated positive-frequency branches, root intervals and norms. Two integrations by parts give O_g(k^-2) for each fixed polynomial; self-adjointness supplies O_p,c(k^-4) for compatible polynomials. The boundary identities 4m(4m-5) and 4m(4m-3) hold for every m>=2, including m=2. Repeating the integration identities gives the stated nonzero normalized leading terms and O_m(k^-6) remainders. Consequently each nonaffine member has a spectral tail comparable to sum k^(2s-8), proving convergence exactly for s<7/2 and harmonic divergence at equality.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "R6-four-trace-core-and-density",
					"reason": "Leading-degree elimination proves span{p_n}=Pi intersect D(Kc). The product-domain definition gives D(Kc^2)={f in Sobolev H4:Bf=B(f'')=0}. Direct evaluation gives the displayed four-trace matrix with determinant 15360, hence a bounded polynomial right inverse. Approximating f^(4) in L2 and integrating four times gives H4 approximation with convergent traces; subtracting the fixed right inverse of the residual makes the correction vanish and yields graph-norm approximation. Spectral cutoffs and ||u||s<=c^((s-4)/2)||u||4 then prove density for every 0<=s<7/2. The example p6-(7/2)p4 satisfies all four traces despite its individual summands lying outside Hc4. No upward transfer from Hc3 or stronger basis conclusion is needed.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "R6-range-propagation-and-inherited-obligations",
					"reason": "All 77 supplied input hashes matched initially and after verification. Current card source and dependency bindings resolve to supplied matching snapshots. The cofinite, quotient and stability sources match the hashes recorded in the supplied previous card versions; their relevant arguments and restrictions remain consistent with the new window. Negative-order completion, both low modes, genuine versus algebraic inverses, and polynomial-domain distinctions remain correct. Historical unresolved-window text is superseded by the current proof, not treated as a current defect or as evidence for the new theorem.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				}
